 "sentences": [
  "The word nepotism comes from cardinal-nephews.",
  "A cardinal-nephew was a relative elevated by a pope.",
  "This practice began in the Middle Ages.",
  "It reached its peak in the 16th and 17th centuries.",
  "Renaissance popes who created cardinals appointed relatives.",
  "The practice ended in 1692 with a papal bull.",
  "It was abolished after seven centuries of history."
